{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/test/clax.test.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T19:56:33.607481Z","id":"c61d6d1f9c7948c694775b05ee674a4cdc54b11b238e79588f23c030534e891c","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Duplicate of 4031affc752b: both re-anchored ec23bc9083f7 (this one on the multi-person branch, 4031affc752b on main), so the rebase onto main kept two live copies; the re-anchor of 4031affc752b at plugins/pi/test/clax.test.ts:801:849 carries the thread.","supersedes":"76bc3b2e59d196fa3231ee3cc30080f99335b99dd70605f25ac92af763c4e52c","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/test/clax.test.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:20:43.745104Z","id":"9bab01321405af8ab4a5e8a9d9d4b0fdc7679af7c60714b3c017cf47098ebb8c","body":{"detail":"Seen once on 2026-10-13 in a full vitest run of plugins/pi while a cargo build ran beside it (expect.poll(() => polls.length).toBe(1) received 7 within its 10 s). Alone, and in the next two full runs, it passed. trackPolls counts every DaemonClient's inject polls, so a poll of another loop, or a quick series of early returns paced by injectRetryMs (250 ms), would both count; which one this was is not known. Compare 6fab3d3d, a count flake in another tier 5 test.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1148},"end":{"line":1181},"content_hash":"f569dab282bd8b4473edd666b40890f77340398bd460c8470e07f8ecb45763df"},"summary":"Unexplained flake: 'the injection loop never starts a stopped daemon, and resumes when one is back' saw 7 inject polls where it waits for 1","tags":["tests","flaky","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/test/clax.test.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:21:22.869860Z","id":"4ba26f23a8696a930bf9a230e1028efabd9e49c15ddf0402a4875ae0367d2d34","body":{"detail":"target/gates.log of the toolpath-audit worktree at bf1180d: AssertionError expected length 2 but got 4 at clax.test.ts:800. Not reproduced in 32 runs of the tier 5 tests under 8-way parallel load, nor in 5 runs of the Pi lane alone and 5 under 20 busy processes. trackPolls now records each poll's tier and client and the counts assert on pollsSeen(polls), so the next failure names the extra polls; the fake daemon now answers tool-call reports, so the case no longer waits 3 s at shutdown (that wait came after the failing assertion and is not the cause).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":805},"end":{"line":853},"content_hash":"23af039100f651dd8f641ac591f9f6101ff35dcdcbb2e0ab6f25c430e61d01ac"},"suggested_fix":"On the next failure, read which tier and client made the extra polls from the assertion's diff.","summary":"Unexplained flake: 'tier 5 holds… (parked 2000 ms)' saw 4 inject polls instead of 2 in the quality gate run of bf1180d","supersedes":"6fab3d3d295177fa27bee305a62521fb2e7f68ee5a608bd55fcf63a3941a35c6","tags":["review","tests","flaky","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/test/remote.test.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:16:36.715770Z","id":"abaa6166bb98a421ccb69bf41c47a8f23861f42a12c7913e384fc42a1341d747","body":{"detail":"`ahead` is computed once (line 321); learnOffset (plugins/pi/src/remote.ts:183) takes round(Date) - floor(now), so every second between computing `ahead` and the answer lowers the offset by one, and the Date header's whole seconds take up to one more. On a machine with a load average near 200 a vitest worker can stall that long.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":320},"end":{"line":337},"content_hash":"a680bdb4d36fac7242cc2ac83e70203561ed40f3b9ea7d47b7d987ae59ae035b"},"suggested_fix":"Let the fake daemon compute the Date when it answers (Date.now() + 100_000 inside the handler), or assert the offset within a wider bound.","summary":"The stale-request test asserts |offset - 100| <= 2, with the daemon's Date fixed before two servers start and the home is connected: a stall of about 1-2 s before the request is answered fails it","tags":["review","tests","flake","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
